## Security Guidelines

### Supabase Security Best Practices

- **Row-Level Security (RLS)**

  - Implement RLS policies for all tables
  - Never disable RLS unless absolutely necessary
  - Example policy:
    ```sql
    -- Users can only read/write their own data
    CREATE POLICY "Users can manage their own profiles"
    ON profiles
    FOR ALL
    USING (auth.uid() = user_id)
    WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);
    ```

- **Authentication**

  - Use Supabase Auth for all authentication needs
  - Implement appropriate session management
  - Set up proper password policies
  - Consider enabling 2FA for admin accounts

- **Edge Functions Security**

  - Validate and sanitize all inputs
  - Use proper error handling to avoid leaking sensitive information
  - Check authentication and authorization in each function
  - Keep environment variables secure

- **Frontend Security**
  - Never store sensitive information in localStorage
  - Implement proper CSRF protection
  - Use Content Security Policy (CSP) headers
  - Sanitize user inputs to prevent XSS attacks

### Data Protection

- Encrypt sensitive data at rest when necessary
- Limit the exposure of user IDs and other identifiers
- Implement proper access controls
- Follow data protection regulations (GDPR, CCPA, etc.)

## Performance Considerations

### React Performance

- Use React.memo for components that render often but rarely change
- Implement virtualization for long lists (react-window or react-virtualized)
- Code-splitting with React.lazy() and Suspense
- Use proper key props in lists (unique and stable identifiers)

### TanStack Query Optimization

- Configure appropriate staleTime and cacheTime for queries
- Use selective invalidation of queries
- Implement optimistic updates for a better UX
- Set up prefetching for anticipated data needs

### Supabase Performance

- Create appropriate indexes on frequently queried columns
- Use Row-Level Security (RLS) policies effectively
- Optimize select statements (avoid SELECT \* when possible)
- Use foreign key constraints for data integrity
- Consider using Supabase Views for complex queries

### General Optimizations

- Implement proper pagination for large datasets
- Use debounce for search inputs and other frequent events
- Lazy load images and components
- Minimize bundle size with tree-shaking and code-splitting
